+### Operator-approved mapping import
+
+A2a owns `scripts/meeting-authority/import-authority-mappings.ts` and its
+adjacent test. The importer is the only A2 path that creates mapping rows. It
+accepts an out-of-repository JSON manifest with exact source tenant/user IDs,
+exact internal tenant/user IDs, `verificationMethod`, opaque `evidenceRef`,
+`verifiedByActorId`, and `verifiedAt`, plus an operator-reviewed SHA-256 supplied
+separately on the command line. It never accepts email, provider subject,
+display labels, or an equality shortcut.
+
+Before writing, one transaction verifies every manifest source tenant/user pair
+exists in `meetings`, every target tenant/user pair exists internally, the
+verifying actor is an active human admin in that exact internal tenant, the
+target user has current active organization membership, and tenant/principal
+rows agree. Duplicate identical active rows are `alreadyPresent`; a missing
+source/target, duplicate conflicting manifest row, existing conflicting row,
+ambiguous pair, revoked mapping, hash mismatch, or inactive approver aborts the
+whole import with no writes. Source pairs omitted from the approved manifest
+remain unmapped and the later backfill quarantines them as `mapping_missing`.
+
+The exact dry-run and apply commands are:
+
+```text
+bun run scripts/meeting-authority/import-authority-mappings.ts -- --database-url-env MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL --manifest <absolute-approved-json> --expected-sha256 <reviewed-sha256> --dry-run --report <absolute-report-json>
+bun run scripts/meeting-authority/import-authority-mappings.ts -- --database-url-env MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL --manifest <absolute-approved-json> --expected-sha256 <reviewed-sha256> --apply --report <absolute-report-json>
+```
+
+The redacted report records manifest hash, approver actor, evidence refs, and
+sorted `inserted|alreadyPresent|rejected` counts plus opaque source/internal IDs;
+it contains no email, provider identity, labels, meeting content, or credentials.
+Apply must match the reviewed dry-run hash and is idempotent only for the exact
+same verified mapping rows. Backfill cannot start until apply completes with
+zero rejected rows and a second dry-run reports zero inserts.
+
 `meetings.tenant_id` and `meetings.owner_user_id` are explicitly source-system
 identifiers. They are never assumed equal to `tenants.id` or `users.id`.
 Backfill must first resolve the active tenant mapping, then the exact active
